+### Selection in vertical Expressive menus
+
+Use `Theme::vertical_choice_menu` to add checked states to an anchored
+menu. Pass up to three `VerticalChoiceMenuGroup` values. Give each group a
+stable ID and a visible name. Use `VerticalMenuSelection::Commands` for
+ordinary actions. For `Single`, pass the stable ID of the selected row or
+`None`. For `Multiple`, pass the stable IDs of the checked rows.
+
+Keep the selection in application state. On an accepted single choice,
+store its ID as the group's selection. Invoking the current selection
+leaves it selected and sends no action. On a multiple choice, toggle that
+row's checked state and keep the menu open. Arrow keys change focus.
+Activation changes selection. Disabled choices keep their checked state
+and cannot send actions.
+
+Selected choices use a different shape and color and show a checkmark.
+Single choices expose a radio menu item with its checked state. Multiple
+choices expose a checkbox menu item. The checkmark has no separate action.
